n genre, intertwining themes of survival and environmental catastrophe with a steampunk aesthetic. Set in a post-apocalyptic world where cities move on wheels and consume each other for resources, the narrative unfolds in a speculative future that resonates with contemporary anxieties about environmental degradation and societal collapse. Reeve's imaginative construction of a world where the remnants of civilization are embodied in predatory urban machines invites readers to reflect on the implications of unchecked industrialization and resource depletion.

